This repository is a MODIFIED VERSION of E-Ink Launcher.
Baseline: master branch, versionName 0.1.8.6 / versionCode 30,
commit 155738c ("feat: 添加应用排序设置").

Modifications, all made in 2026:

1. Grid layout now supports items spanning multiple cells.
   - model/AppDataCenter.java: new Placement (col/row/span) and a
     first-fit page packing algorithm; folders occupy 2x2, apps 1x1.
   - widgets/EInkLauncherView.java: onMeasure/onLayout laid out by span;
     per-cell grid-line background chosen by block position.

2. Folders (new feature).
   - model/FolderStore.java (new): JSON persistence of folders and
     manual order in SharedPreferences "launcherFolders".
   - widgets/FolderIconView.java (new): draws a 3x3 preview of up to
     nine icons on a Canvas; hit-testing decides "launch child app"
     versus "open folder".
   - FolderDialog.java (new): folder contents dialog (launch, remove,
     rename, dissolve).

3. Manual icon ordering (new feature).
   - widgets/AppItemBinder.java: order mode, selection highlight.
   - Launcher.java / SettingFragment.java: entry point and callbacks.
   - AppSortComparator: new SORT_MANUAL mode.

4. Landscape support.
   - Launcher.java: applyGrid() swaps columns/rows in landscape;
     onConfigurationChanged() re-applies the grid in place.
   - AndroidManifest.xml: configChanges added to the Launcher activity.

5. Swipe-to-change-page fix (upstream bug).
   - widgets/EInkLauncherView.java: the view now consumes touch events,
     page changes are triggered on ACTION_MOVE, child touches are
     cancelled so a swipe does not also click an icon.

6. Icon loading.
   - LineIcons.java (new): optional per-package line icons from
     assets/icons/<package>.png, cached as Bitmap (a new BitmapDrawable
     is created per use to avoid shared-bounds corruption).

7. Minor additions: folder-name toggle (Config.KEY_SHOW_FOLDER_NAME),
   new strings/arrays, layout changes in launcher_item.xml and
   launcher_activity.xml.

Third-party assets:
   app/src/main/assets/icons/*.png are derived from Arcticons
   (https://github.com/Donnnno/Arcticons), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
   They are optional: if an icon is missing the launcher falls back to
   the system icon.
